---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
const entries = Object.entries(import.meta.glob("../../content/work/*.md", { eager: true }))
  .map(([path, mod]) => ({ slug: path.split("/").pop().replace(/\.md$/, ""), ...mod.frontmatter }))
  .filter((item) => item.category === "sounds" && item.status !== "draft")
  .sort((a,b) => String(b.date || "").localeCompare(String(a.date || "")));
---
<SiteLayout title="Sounds, ScribbledToday" description="Poetry with handpan, sound healing, singing, songwriting and bhajan jamming.">
  <main>
    <div class="page-hero"><div class="eyebrow">02 / Listen</div><h1>Where Sound Finds <em>Expression</em></h1><p>For me, sound is more than music. It's a way to express, connect, create and sometimes simply be present.</p></div>
    <section class="section sound-copy">
      <p>My journey with sound takes different forms. Sometimes through singing, sometimes through the gentle resonance of a handpan, sometimes through poetry accompanied by music, and sometimes through creating spaces where people can pause and reconnect through sound.</p>
      <p>Each has its own character, its own rhythm and its own way of reaching people. Here are a few ways sound finds its expression in my world.</p>
      <div class="sound-part"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / Words in rhythm</div><h2>Poetry & Handpan</h2><p>Sometimes poetry finds its expression through words. Sometimes, it finds another dimension through music. I enjoy performing my poetry accompanied by the handpan, bringing together spoken words and flowing melodies. It's an intimate form of expression where rhythm, silence and words come together to create something a little different. The handpan adds another layer to the experience, allowing the words to breathe and the emotions to travel beyond the lines themselves.</p></div><img src="/images/IMG_1954.jpg" alt="Performing poetry with handpan at a music festival" loading="lazy"/></div>
      <div class="sound-part reverse"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / Pause & listen</div><h2>Sound Healing</h2><p>One of the most meaningful parts of my journey with sound is facilitating group sound healing sessions. These sessions are an invitation to slow down, step away from the noise of everyday life and spend some time with yourself. Through the resonant sounds of instruments and an immersive listening experience, I create spaces where people can pause, relax and reconnect. For me, it's about creating an experience where sound is not just heard, but felt.</p></div><img src="/images/IMG_5593.jpg" alt="Sound instruments arranged for a group sound session" loading="lazy"/></div>
      <div class="sound-part"><div><div class="eyebrow">03 / Voice & melody</div><h2>Singing & Songwriting</h2><p>Singing has always been an important part of how I express myself. I enjoy exploring songs, melodies and songwriting, with a special connection to Hindi music. There's something beautiful about giving a melody a voice, or finding the right words for a tune that has been playing in your head. Over time, this journey has also led me to release my own music. One such release is <em>Sannata</em>, a piece of my musical expression that I'm happy to share.</p><a class="btn primary" href="https://open.spotify.com/track/2iDklGtwlPzfXhvDvcAvCc?si=a23e1fac78554ee1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Listen to Sannata on Spotify ↗</a></div><img src="/images/03b3ca75-c94b-4666-bf2e-a137d31b4f51.JPG" alt="Singing during a live performance" loading="lazy"/></div>
      <div class="sound-part reverse"><div><div class="eyebrow">04 / Shared devotion</div><h2>Bhajan Jamming</h2><p>Some musical moments don't need a stage or an audience. Bhajan jamming is one such experience. Familiar devotional melodies, voices coming together and the simple joy of singing in the moment. I enjoy the spontaneity of these gatherings, where music isn't about performance or perfection. It's about participation, devotion and the happiness of sharing a song.</p></div><img src="/images/16a14b1c-37d2-4647-97d0-16c8b2dcbeb1.JPG" alt="Singing during a festive gathering" loading="lazy"/></div>
      <p class="sound-close">Different expressions, different sounds, but one common thread: the joy of creating and sharing something through sound.</p>
    </section>
    {entries.length ? <section class="section"><div class="eyebrow">More from the sound space</div><h2 class="section-title">Sound notes</h2><div class="card-grid">{entries.map((entry) => <a class="work-card" href={`/work/${entry.slug}/`}><div class="card-meta"><span>{entry.date || "Sound"}</span><span>↗</span></div><div><h2>{entry.title}</h2><p>{entry.excerpt || "A sound experience from ScribbledToday."}</p></div></a>)}</div></section> : null}
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
.sound-copy{max-width:930px;margin:auto}.sound-copy>p{font-size:16px;line-height:1.9;color:var(--muted);max-width:820px}.sound-part{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr .95fr;gap:38px;align-items:center;padding:42px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:32px}.sound-part.reverse img{order:-1}.sound-part h2{font:500 clamp(36px,4vw,48px)/1 'Cormorant Garamond',serif;margin:10px 0 15px}.sound-part p{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;line-height:1.9}.sound-part img{width:100%;height:330px;object-fit:cover;border:1px solid var(--line)}.sound-part .btn{margin-top:12px}.sound-close{padding:30px 0;font:400 26px 'Caveat',cursive;color:var(--accent)!important}@media(max-width:700px){.sound-part{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:18px}.sound-part.reverse img{order:0}.sound-part img{height:260px}}
</style>